<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch NBM-Amstelland may sell Sesam unit.</title>
<headline>Dutch NBM-Amstelland may sell Sesam unit.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch construction firm NBM-Amstelland NV said on Thursday its unit Cementbouw Handel &amp; Industrie BV was in talks with Cecem Holding BV about the sale of Sesam BV, a grain storage unit.</p>
<p>No financial details were given on the deal. NBM said both parties were expecting to reach an agreement.</p>
<p>Sesam rents units for the storage of grain and animal feed.</p>
<p>NBM-Amstelland said another party had been interested in acquiring Sesam but the talks had not been succesful.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 500</p>
</text>
